{"path":"ranges/join_with_view/iterator/operator_cmp","title":"operator==(ranges::join_with_view::iterator)","titleHtml":"operator==<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">(ranges::join_with_view::<i>iterator</i>)</span>","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/ranges/join_with_view/iterator/operator_cmp","section":"ranges","kind":"page","summary":"Compares whether the iterators x and y are equal. They only compare equal if their outer iterators and inner iterators compare equal respectively.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx23\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">friend</span> <span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span> <span class=\"kw4\">bool</span> operator<span class=\"sy1\">==</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <span class=\"coMULTI\">/*iterator*/</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> x, <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <span class=\"coMULTI\">/*iterator*/</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> y <span class=\"br0\">)</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; requires <a href=\"/w/cpp/types/is_reference\"><span class=\"kw488\">std::<span class=\"me2\">is_reference_v</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>InnerBase<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> <span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<a href=\"/w/cpp/concepts/equality_comparable\"><span class=\"kw2968\">std::<span class=\"me2\">equality_comparable</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/iterator_t\"><span class=\"kw2908\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">iterator_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>Base<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<a href=\"/w/cpp/concepts/equality_comparable\"><span class=\"kw2968\">std::<span class=\"me2\">equality_comparable</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/iterator_t\"><span class=\"kw2908\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">iterator_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>InnerBase<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx23\">(since C++23)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Compares whether the iterators <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">x</span></code> and <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">y</span></code> are equal. They only compare equal if their <a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/join_with_view/iterator\">outer iterators</a> and <a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/join_with_view/iterator\">inner iterators</a> compare equal respectively.\n</p><p>This function  is not visible to ordinary <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/unqualified_lookup\">unqualified</a> or <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/qualified_lookup\">qualified lookup</a>, and can only be found by <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/adl\">argument-dependent lookup</a> when <code>std::ranges::join_with_view::<i>iterator</i></code> ﻿<code>&lt;Const&gt;</code> is an associated class of the arguments.\n</p><p>The <code>!=</code> operator is <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/default_comparisons#Other_defaulted_comparison_operators\">synthesized</a> from <code>operator==</code>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> x, y\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> iterators to compare\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">x.</span><code><i><a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/join_with_view/iterator#outer_it\">outer_it_</a></i></code><code>&nbsp;</code><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy1\">==</span> y.</span><code><i><a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/join_with_view/iterator#outer_it\">outer_it_</a></i></code><code>&nbsp;</code><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span> x.</span><code><i><a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/join_with_view/iterator#inner_it\">inner_it_</a></i></code><code>&nbsp;</code><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy1\">==</span> y.</span><code><i><a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/join_with_view/iterator#inner_it\">inner_it_</a></i></code></code>\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/join_with_view/sentinel/operator_cmp\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>operator==</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx23\">(C++23)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>   compares a sentinel with an iterator returned from <a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/join_with_view/begin\"><code>join_with_view::begin</code></a>  <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"ranges","title":"Ranges library (since C++20)"},{"path":"ranges/join_with_view","title":"std::ranges::views::join_with, std::ranges::join_with_view"},{"path":"ranges/join_with_view/iterator","title":"std::ranges::join_with_view<V,Pattern>::iterator"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"operator==(ranges::join_with_view::iterator)","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration; revisions: since C++23. Compares whether the iterators x and y are equal."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"x, y"},{"label":"Return value","note":"x.outer_it_ == y.outer_it_ && x.inner_it_ == y.inner_it_"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"operator==","note":"compares a sentinel with an iterator returned from join_with_view::begin"}]}]},"standards":["C++23"],"wordCount":107,"codeBlockCount":0}
